  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nSub-PR 2 of 2 for #4176 (K2, the guide stage). Sub-PR 1 (the ring and row planners) merged as PR #4189. This PR adds the medial line, the trace of a chain and the helix guide planners. No old planner changes. No planner calls the new code yet, so with the default switch the output is identical. The baseline pins of the side branch stay green.\n\n## Public surface\n\n- `guide::MedialPlanner`: the medial axis of the cutter-centre area, family `Medial`. Refusals: `NO_MEDIAL`, `NARROW_NECK`, `MEDIAL_TOO_FINE`, `NOT_MEDIAL`.\n- `guide::TracePlanner` on the new region kind `KernelRegion::Chains(ChainRegion)`, built by `chain_region(sel, plane, tool, keep_out)`. Refusals: `NOT_A_CHAIN`, `NOT_TRACE`, `TRACE_COLLAPSES`, `TRACE_KEPT_OUT`.\n- `TraceOffset`: above zero is to the left of the chain. A closed chain is read counter-clockwise, so its left is its inside.\n- `RingsChoice` with a circle: exact circle rings of a hole. Each ring has its `Circle` and a carrier polygon with a chord count from the tolerance (#3756). Refusal: `CIRCLE_NOT_REGION`. `CIRCLE_NOT_YET` is removed.\n- `GuideChoice::Helix(HelixChoice)` with `Hand`, and `guide::HelixPlanner`. Refusals: `TOO_MANY_TURNS`, `HELIX_OUTSIDE`, `HELIX_TOO_FINE`, `NOT_HELIX`.\n- `Curve::lead()` and `Lead`. `Curve::helix` is the checked constructor (`NOT_ON_HELIX`). `Curve::new` refuses the helix family (`HELIX_NEEDS_LEAD`).\n- `Guides` plans each family. `FAMILY_NOT_YET` is removed. The area planners refuse a chain region with `NOT_AN_AREA`.\n- New in `camcraft-geometry`, each in its own file:\n  - `Region::medial_axis`, `Region::medial_spacing`, `MedialAxis`, `MedialCurve` (`geo2d/medial.rs`, with a crate-private Delaunay in `geo2d/delaunay.rs`);\n  - `offset_side` and `SidePiece` (`geo2d/side_offset.rs`).\n\nThe guide choices moved from `guide.rs` to `guide/choice.rs` with no change. The public paths stay the same by re-export.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `camcraft-geometry` lib:\n  - `geo2d::medial::tests::*` (slot, rectangle, annulus, input order, refusals, a touching neck);\n  - `geo2d::delaunay::tests::*` (a co-circular grid, scattered points);\n  - `geo2d::side_offset::tests::*`.\n- `camcraft-pathkernel` `laws`:\n  - `guide_medial`, `guide_trace`, `guide_helix`;\n  - `guide_laws`: the medial planner, the circle rings and the helix run through `kit::run` and hold L1 to L4;\n  - `guide_trace::the_trace_holds_l1_to_l4`.\n- `camcraft-motion` `pass_start_levels::kernel_guides`: agreement with the #4153 goldens of Trace, Engrave, Slot, Circular, Bore and Thread (the guide geometry only). Each difference is named in the file header and in the decisions file.\n\n## Gates on the final head 2e7f78856, base `origin/side/path-kernel` 25f3838db\n\n- `cargo check --tests` for pathkernel, geometry and motion, one at a time: clean.\n- Clippy `-D warnings` for geometry, pathkernel and motion: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel`: the geometry change makes it a full batch plan. Result: 1223 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 88.9 min. This includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` and clippy.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 7 steps, 0 failed.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/4176-kernel-guides-medial-trace-helix.md`. The main decisions:\n- The medial line is the theta-pruned Voronoi medial axis. It is not a port of the old single-channel spine.\n- A chain region holds the chains of a trace.\n- The circle rings use the stepover from the wall. The Bore recipe gives `rc / count` to get the old even rings.\n- There is one helix for each choice. The hand is geometry, and the direction of travel stays with stage 4.\n\n## Review fix (head 33c116cfa): later stages keep the data of a family\n\nThe review found that the K4 order stage reversed a curve with `Curve::new`, which refuses the helix family. Commit 6aa630fee closes the finding with one rule for the class: a later stage that restarts, reverses or replaces a curve makes it again through the constructor of the curve's family (`Curve::with_points`: `Curve::helix` with the same circle and lead, else `Curve::new` with the same circle), or it refuses by a reason of its own stage.\n\n- Order: a helix always runs down its lead. A reversal also turns it up its lead, so the stage reverses a helix only when the guide set holds it upward. The hand sets the side of the material. A direction that the hand does not give is named by the order note `HELIX_HAND_SETS_DIRECTION`. A failed rebuild is the order reason `NOT_REVERSIBLE`.\n- Load (K3): constant engagement inserts passes only before a ring (`NOT_A_RING` else). Trochoidal loops leave a curve with a lead, an exact circle or a changing depth as it is (`SHAPE_KEPT`). A refused rebuild is `SET_NOT_KEPT`. Loops that make no curve are `LOOPS_NOT_A_CURVE`.\n- Link and entry make no new curve.\n- Pins: `later_stages::each_guide_family_keeps_its_data_or_is_refused_by_the_stage_in_each_later_stage` (7 rows x 13 stage cells) and `later_stages::the_order_stage_runs_a_helix_down_its_lead_and_names_a_direction_that_its_hand_does_not_give`. Both are red with the old reversal (`HELIX_NEEDS_LEAD` from the Guide stage) and green with the fix. `guide_trace::each_later_stage_refuses_the_chain_region_of_a_trace_by_name` has three new load stage rows (`LOAD_NOT_PLANAR`).\n- Merge of `side/path-kernel` df9ec30b6 (PRs #4265 and #4253) in 7922d0c6c: no conflicts, empty remerge-diff (class SAME).\n- Checks on 6aa630fee: `cargo check --tests` for pathkernel, geometry and motion (one at a time); pathkernel `laws` 157 passed; geometry all suites green; motion `pass_start_levels` `kernel_guides`, `kernel_rings`, `kernel_baseline` 22 passed; motion `kernel_laws` 29 passed and 1 known red of the base (`k3_load::kernel_load_control_round_the_disc_and_the_dog_bone`, 337 and 77 against 334 and 74, fixed by PRs #4279 and #4275); clippy `-D warnings` on the three crates clean. The quick plan is a full batch (1223 steps) because of geometry. The geometry change is one doc sentence, so the batch was not run again; the full batch ran green on 33c116cfa.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A trace through all the kernel stages. The entry stage refuses a region that is not an area today. Follow-up #4236.\n- Engrave with an avoid item against its golden. The old keep-out comes from an avoid item with its own pad.\n- The fig8 fixture, and medial lines of large areas at a fine tolerance. The sample count is limited to 200000, and above that limit the planner refuses by name.\n- The K4 branch (#4177). This PR stays out of `order*` and `link*`. Its geometry is in new files. Only the module list of `geo2d.rs` can need a manual merge.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #4176\n\n",
